---
description: Check this rule when creating cards
alwaysApply: true
---

When you create a card, if an image is provided, optimise the image as a webp image with 75% quality with image magick, then delete the source image.

When a **golden video** is provided for a card:

1. Place the source video under `public/card-videos/<slug>_original.mp4`.
2. Encode a game-ready version beside it (4s, muted, 640px wide, H.264):

```bash
ffmpeg -y -i public/card-videos/<slug>_original.mp4 -t 4 -an \
  -vf "scale=640:-2" -c:v libx264 -pix_fmt yuv420p -crf 28 -preset slow -movflags +faststart \
  public/card-videos/<slug>.mp4
```

3. On the card seed, set both:
   - `imageUrl: "/card-covers/.../<slug>.webp"` (poster / normal art)
   - `goldenVideoUrl: "/card-videos/<slug>.mp4"` (golden animated art)
4. Presence of `goldenVideoUrl` makes the card eligible for golden pack drops.
5. Delete the original video.

After creating cards, always update "cards.md", with `yarn generate:cards-md`
